---
title: Oreo Cookie Crumble
description: Salted, buttery Oreo crumbs to spoon over custard or ice cream.
tags: [chocolate, topping]
course: dessert
source:
  name: delish
  url: https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/recipes/a56559/oreo-crumble-recipe/
adapted: true
---

Melt the @unsalted butter{56%g}(4 tbsp, 1/2 stick) over medium-low heat in a #small saucepan{}.

Remove the cream filling from the @Oreo cookies{85%g}(about 1 cup, measured crushed) (with a knife, not one's tongue).

Add the @&Oreo cookies{} and @coarse salt{1/4%tsp} into a #food processor{}.

Begin to slowly drizzle the melted @&unsalted butter{} into the food processor while pulsing the ingredients.

Stop pulsing when all the butter is mixed in AND the cookie crumble pieces are the size of dimes or small peas.

Store in an #airtight container{} in the fridge (for up to a week).
